#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:3
msgid "Installing applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:5
msgid ""
":doc:`getting-started` walked through the ``install`` → ``list`` → ``run`` → "
"``uninstall`` cycle with the toy ``pycowsay`` package. This tutorial repeats "
"it with a real tool so you can see how a package's name and its apps differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:10
msgid "Install a tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:12
msgid "Install `HTTPie <https://httpie.io/>`_, a command-line HTTP client:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:14
msgid ""
"$ pipx install httpie\n"
"  installed package httpie 3.2.4, installed using Python 3.12.3\n"
"  These apps are now available\n"
"    - http\n"
"    - httpie\n"
"    - https\n"
"  These manual pages are now available\n"
"    - man1/http.1\n"
"    - man1/httpie.1\n"
"    - man1/https.1\n"
"done! ✨ 🌟 ✨"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:28
msgid ""
"pipx creates a virtual environment, installs the ``httpie`` package into it, "
"and exposes the apps it declares on your ``PATH``. Note that the package is "
"``httpie`` but the commands are ``http``, ``httpie``, and ``https``: one "
"package, three apps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:34
msgid ""
"To install a tool for every user on the system, pass ``--global``. See :doc:"
"`Configure paths <../how-to/configure-paths>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:39
msgid "See what you got"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:41
msgid ""
"$ pipx list\n"
"venvs are in /home/user/.local/share/pipx/venvs\n"
"apps are exposed on your $PATH at /home/user/.local/bin\n"
"manual pages are exposed at /home/user/.local/share/man\n"
"shell completions are exposed at /home/user/.local/share\n"
"   package httpie 3.2.4, installed using Python 3.12.3\n"
"    - http\n"
"    - httpie\n"
"    - https\n"
"    - man1/http.1\n"
"    - man1/httpie.1\n"
"    - man1/https.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:58
msgid "Run it and verify"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:60
msgid "Call one of the exposed apps to confirm the install:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:62
msgid ""
"$ http --version\n"
"3.2.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:67
msgid ""
"If the version prints, the app is on your ``PATH`` and ready to use. "
"(Missing? Run ``pipx ensurepath`` and open a new terminal, then see :doc:"
"`Troubleshoot <../how-to/troubleshoot>`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:72
msgid "Hold back fresh releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:74
msgid ""
"A brand-new release is the one most likely to be broken or compromised. "
"Install the next tool a week behind the index:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:76
msgid ""
"$ pipx install --cooldown 7 black\n"
"  installed package black 24.8.0, installed using Python 3.12.3\n"
"  These apps are now available\n"
"    - black\n"
"    - blackd\n"
"done! ✨ 🌟 ✨"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:85
msgid ""
"pipx remembers the number, so later upgrades of ``black`` keep the same "
"seven-day lag without you repeating the flag. Set ``PIPX_COOLDOWN=7`` in "
"your shell profile to get the same lag for every tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:90
msgid "Learn more"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:92
msgid "``pipx install`` has more to offer once you outgrow the basics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:94
msgid ""
":doc:`Expose apps <../how-to/expose-apps>`: hide or reveal commands with "
"``expose`` / ``unexpose``, and pull apps out of dependencies with ``--"
"include-deps``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:96
msgid ""
":doc:`Tool manifests <../how-to/tool-manifest>`: manage a set of tools with "
"a ``pipx.toml`` manifest and PEP 751 lock files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:98
msgid ""
":doc:`Run scripts <../how-to/run-scripts>`: install a local PEP 723 script "
"as a managed app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:99
msgid ""
":doc:`Use the uv backend <../how-to/use-uv-backend>`: swap pip for uv to "
"resolve and install faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:100
msgid ""
":doc:`Standalone Python <../how-to/standalone-python>`: install against a "
"specific Python version, downloading one if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/install-applications.rst:102
msgid ""
":doc:`Dependency cooldown <../how-to/dependency-cooldown>`: set the release-"
"age lag once with ``PIPX_COOLDOWN``."
msgstr ""
